# id | cadence | last done | what to run   (format: the header of ~/bin/maintenance)
# card/hls.min.js is a copy of hls.js (Apache-2.0), the full build: the light one can't play 4K clips.
hls-js | 90d | 2026-11-21 | npm view hls.js version; if newer than 1.6.13: replace card/hls.min.js from cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/hls.js@X/dist/hls.min.js, play a 4K clip and a still-downloading clip in Chrome, and update the version in this line
# custom_components/reolink is a copy of one Home Assistant release; a newer HA may have changed what it replaces.
reolink-integration | 30d | 2026-11-21 | compare the Home Assistant version in use to "version" in custom_components/reolink/manifest.json; if HA is newer: bin/integration-refresh <that version>, drop any change of ours HA now covers, then deploy and play a clip
# One-off (camera-card#3, started 2026-11-27): review the first Auto-Tune run, then delete this line.
autotune-review | 2d | 2026-11-27 | GET /api/reolink/tuning (the card's Auto-tune view) and home-assistant.log "Tuning ch": where each camera settled, false alarms per camera, the day's Gemini count in camera_alerts.yaml.count; use them to pick monthly budgets for #19 and add the findings there
# Wrong descriptions flagged on the card (camera-card#22) roll off the NVR after about a month.
description-reports | 14d | 2026-11-28 | bin/testdata reports; file each open one (save_keyframes, bin/testdata import) and label it as in #14 before the NVR overwrites it
